+/// How many compositor handoffs keep their decoder frame alive.
+///
+/// A compositor handoff exports only a descriptor: the two plane offsets, the
+/// strides and the dma-buf fds the decoder opened for them. Nothing here keeps
+/// those fds open afterwards. The caller that receives the descriptor is Qt's
+/// frame token, and the token is released as soon as the render pass that
+/// carries it ends, which drops the AVFrame that `video/ffmpeg.rs` retained for
+/// the frame and lets v4l2-request retire the output surface it decoded into.
+/// The compositor has not read the request yet: libwayland queued the `add` and
+/// `create_immed` pair when the stream surface sent it, and Weston imports the
+/// planes only when that message reaches it. A retired surface makes the import
+/// fail (`Failed to import plane 0 as R8` plus a protocol error that closes the
+/// stream window) and makes this crate's CPU copy fail with `Bad file
+/// descriptor (os error 9)` when the copy runs behind the decoder. Holding the
+/// frames whose descriptors went out for a fixed window keeps the surface, and
+/// the fds it named, alive until the queued copy and the compositor import have
+/// finished. The window is a ring, so the decoder is never asked to hold more
+/// than this many surfaces at a time: 24 frames is 0.4 s of video at 60 fps, a
+/// round trip the compositor cannot fall behind by.
+const COMPOSITOR_HANDOFF_RETAINED: usize = 24;
